            "summary": "A 404 Media investigation published 21 July 2026 identified ISBNdb as a broker marketing bulk print-book acquisition to AI developers, pitching pre-2022 books as training data free of AI-generated text, with strict NDAs and orders of 1,000 to 1 million books. The only court-proven case of mass destruction is Anthropic's 'Project Panama', unsealed in Bartz v. Anthropic, where a 2025 ruling treated destructive scanning of legally purchased books as fair use.",
