            "keyPoints": [
                "ISBNdb pitches pre-2022 print as structurally free of AI slop: it predates generative text.",
                "Marketing promises a strict NDA on every engagement so identity, strategy and acquisition targets stay hidden.",
                "ISBNdb's own copy concedes the optics problem: 'AI company destroys two million books' is not a sympathetic headline.",
                "Destruction is a cost decision, not a technical one: robots scan fragile books intact at 2,500 pages/hour.",
                "Alsup's fair-use ruling is a district-court decision only; Anthropic settled, so no appellate precedent exists.",
                "The same ruling found Anthropic's library of 7M+ pirated books was not fair use, leading to a $1.5B settlement.",
                "One bookseller told 404 Media weekly sales jumped from under 20 books to several hundred starting April 2026.",
                "Concern centers on rare, foreign-language and out-of-print titles where few copies remain in circulation."
